{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCgrf8UjvJWfJ5DGhJ8Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six amended rows changed meaning, and I would bless each one. In the first approvals, I approved SR-240 and LLR-340 and returned TC-370. The verdict is committed as `98f5e9cd5`, with `WI: WI-926` and the `Loop-Session` trailer, and the commit checks passed.\n\n**Amendment (`VERDICT: MEANING rows=6`), all `[MEANING+BLESS]`:**\n\n| Row(s) | What changed the obligation |\n|---|---|\n| SR-019, LLR-019 | When the kit scripts can't be found, the commit hooks now refuse with exit 1 and name the repair; they never run or skip the floor. Before, a hook that skipped the floor in that case satisfied the text. TC-019 covers this through its whole-file evidence. |\n| SR-020, LLR-020 | The same refusal at push. TC-020's `test_pre_push_honors_kit_scripts_dir` drives it. |\n| LLR-140 | The claim's commit-floor check now runs before its guard refusal and its dispatch lock. The code matches: the check is the claim's first statement. |\n| LLR-300 | The lease take refuses a checkout whose commit floor is inactive, and records no holder. |\n\n**First approval (`OUTCOME: RETURN rows=3`):**\n- **SR-240, APPROVE:**\n  - It is honestly derived from SN-005 through the SECURITY lens: the hat is recorded and the rationale argues it.\n  - It names no file, and its acceptance criteria are observable.\n  - One advisory: it opens with `Where`, but an inactive floor is a fault condition, which reads as `If … then`. The obligation is the same either way.\n- **LLR-340, APPROVE:** its text is a closed contract, the code matches every arm, and each arm has a passing test.\n- **TC-370, RETURN:** all 19 tests it cites exist and pass, but it has three gaps:\n  1. LLR-340's arm that a session launch tells this refusal apart from a blackout refusal has no clause, and its test, `test_through_blackout_does_not_wait_out_a_hooks_refusal`, is uncited.\n  2. It exercises LLR-140 and LLR-300 but doesn't list them in `Verifies`. The test that the claim's refusal comes before the guard is cited by no TC at all.\n  3. Its Method says every route runs with the floor active, but every route case it cites is the inactive one.\n\nThe one `## Dispositions` draft under `## amendment` fixes all three in spine text only: cite and state those arms, add LLR-140 and LLR-300 to `Verifies`, and either cite the route-level active tests that already exist or narrow the Method. Then re-sit TC-370 alone.\n\n**Checks:**\n- I compared every amended cell with `tomllib`. Each keeps its approved text verbatim and adds one sentence.\n- I read the shared check and confirmed every route calls it first.\n- I ran TC-370's evidence plus the uncited tests: 46 passed, 1 skipped (the non-executable-hook case, which only runs on POSIX).\n- The sitting parser accepts the file.\n\n**For the act turn:**\n- Re-attest SR-019, SR-020, LLR-019, LLR-020, LLR-140 and LLR-300.\n- Flip SR-240 and LLR-340 to `Approved`.\n- TC-370 stays `Drafted`.\n\nI edited no registry cell."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":277587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":794,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"fe48d1de-3879-4665-842c-914b71543e40","timestamp":"2026-10-20T02:19:16.962Z","request_id":"req_011CgCgrekAhTwCZz4gpMaTc"}
